Source and build instructions

For an official binary, download the source archive from the release matching
the app version at https://github.com/antimajorana/Nocturne/releases. The tag
is v followed by the version. README_DEV.md, Cargo.lock and the platform build
scripts in that source tree describe how the program was built.

Releases through v0.0.17 were offered under MIT or Apache-2.0. Their grants
continue to apply to the code distributed under them. Copies of those license
texts are included in licenses/Nocturne-legacy-MIT.txt and
licenses/Nocturne-legacy-Apache-2.0.txt.

Third-party material

This product bundles third-party material under its own licenses. The per-file list (what it
is, where it came from, its license status) is in ATTRIBUTION.md.

- The Nocturne icon in assets/brand/ (nocturne-source.png and the icons, cards and banners
  made from it) is Nocturne's own artwork, drawn for this project by its owner (antimajorana,
  2026-11-18). The artwork is NOT covered by the license above. See ATTRIBUTION.md.
- Noto Naskh Arabic, Noto Sans Hebrew, Noto Sans Devanagari and Noto Sans CJK SC
  (assets/fonts/) - SIL Open Font License 1.1, Copyright 2022 The Noto Project Authors
  (Noto Sans CJK SC: Copyright 2014-2021 Adobe, with Reserved Font Name 'Source'). Bundled
  unmodified so non-Latin and right-to-left scripts have glyphs on a machine that has no
  such font installed; each licence text sits beside its font as assets/fonts/OFL-*.txt.
- The KaTeX maths fonts (assets/fonts/katex/) - SIL Open Font License 1.1, Copyright 2009-2010
  Design Science, Inc. and 2014-2018 Khan Academy, with Reserved Font Names KaTeX_*. Bundled
  unmodified so equations draw in real maths fonts; the licence text is
  assets/fonts/katex/OFL-KaTeX.txt, written from the licence strings inside the fonts.
- Microsoft Fluent UI System Icons - MIT License. See licenses/FLUENT_UI_SYSTEM_ICONS_LICENSE.txt.
- mermaid-rs-renderer - MIT License, by its authors, linked into the program to draw Mermaid diagrams.
- RaTeX (ratex-parser, ratex-layout, ratex-types, ratex-font) - MIT License, by the RaTeX
  authors, linked into the program to typeset equations.
- PDF printouts are drawn with the hayro crates (Laurenz Stampfl), used under the MIT License,
  and with substitute fonts from PDFium (Foxit Software Inc. copyright) compiled into the program.
  The notices are in licenses/PDF-RENDERING-NOTICES.txt. See ATTRIBUTION.md.
- OneNote packages (.onepkg) are unpacked with the cab crate (Matthew D. Steele, MIT License),
  which uses lzxd (Lonami Exo, MIT OR Apache-2.0) and byteorder (Andrew Gallant, MIT OR
  Unlicense), linked into the nocturne-import crate.
- JPEG XL pictures are decoded with the jxl-oxide crates (Wonwoo Choi), used under the MIT
  License (they are MIT OR Apache-2.0), linked into the program. They use brotli-decompressor
  (BSD-3-Clause or MIT) and alloc-no-stdlib and alloc-stdlib (BSD-3-Clause), by Daniel Reiter
  Horn and Dropbox, Inc., linked in the same way.
- The vendored eframe and egui-wgpu crates are from egui 0.37.0. Their MIT and
  Apache-2.0 licenses accompany both crate packages and are included in binary
  distributions as licenses/egui-MIT.txt and licenses/egui-Apache-2.0.txt.
- The window also uses the fonts bundled with egui, which carry their own licenses; those ship
  with the egui crates.
- File > Check for updates (desktop builds only) talks to GitHub with the ureq crate (Apache-2.0
  or MIT) over rustls (Apache-2.0, ISC or MIT) and ring (Apache-2.0 and ISC), checks downloads
  with sha2 (Apache-2.0 or MIT) and compares versions with semver (Apache-2.0 or MIT), all linked
  into the program.
- Dependencies are listed in Cargo.lock, each under its own license. A license audit of them
  (for example with cargo deny) has not been run.

The OneNote test corpus under crates/import/tests/fixtures/3p/ retains the licenses
identified in its individual subdirectories and READMEs.

